# Intentionally empty, and it has to exist.
#
# compose.yaml mounts this whole provisioning/ tree read-only over /etc/grafana/provisioning,
# which REPLACES the one in the image — and the image's copy ships empty plugins/ and
# alerting/ directories. Without them Grafana logs, at level=error, on every single boot:
#
#   Failed to read plugin provisioning files from directory ... no such file or directory
#
# Nothing is actually broken by that, which is the problem: an observability stack whose own
# startup prints errors that are fine to ignore is a stack that teaches people to ignore
# errors. The directory is empty because there genuinely are no provisioned plugins; saying
# so in an empty directory is cheaper than explaining the log line to everybody who reads it.
